<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		ReGrowth 2: Aspen: extra wild animal spawns in RG_AspenForest from other animal mods.
		This folder loads with ReGrowth: Core or the old standalone ReGrowth 2: Aspen (see loadFolders.xml).
		Fix 2026-10-25: ReGrowth's 2026-10-25 update moved the Aspen Forest biome (RG_AspenForest) into ReGrowth: Core
		(1.6/Defs/BiomeDefs/Biomes_Aspen.xml). The folder was gated on the standalone mod's packageId alone, so without it every
		add here silently stopped loading. It now loads with either, and each add is a Conditional on the biome's wildAnimals
		existing, so a Core from before the merge (no Aspen biome) gets nothing instead of errors. Rechecked the same day: the
		merged biome lists 32 animals of its own, none of them added here, and no ReGrowth patch adds wild animals to it. The first block's Mythic Ages / Dark Ages entries
		carry their own MayRequire; every other block is gated on its animal mod, and each block is its own operation so one
		failing cannot stop the rest.
		From Too Many Mods' ReGrowthAspen.xml, where it had no setting. Its Alpha Mythology block was dropped (2026-10-13): that
		mod never got a 1.6 build.
		Why the checks matter: a biome that lists a pawn kind that does not exist, or gets the same animal twice (here and in
		the animal's own wildBiomes or another mod's patch), throws when it builds its commonality table
		(BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal), which breaks wild animal spawning in that biome.
		Audited 2026-10-13 (analysis/regrowth_audit.py) against the installed 1.6 mods: every Alpha Animals, Megafauna,
		Vanilla Animals Expanded, Mythic Ages and Dark Ages pawn kind exists, none is already in the biome's own list or lists
		the biome in its race's wildBiomes, no installed mod patches any of them in, and no animal appears twice in this file.
		Not installed here, checked from other sources instead: Dinosauria (spincrus.dinosauria) has no public source. All
		its names match the race defNames that Combat Extended's and Alpha Biomes' Dinosauria patches target; that its pawn
		kinds share those names and that none already lists this biome is unconfirmed.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
				<xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RG_AspenForest"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
				<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RG_AspenForest"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
					<value>
						<DA_DwarvenMuffton MayRequire="Van.Beasts">0.1</DA_DwarvenMuffton>
						<DA_Crestel MayRequire="Van.Beasts">0.05</DA_Crestel>
						<DA_NorthernDrog MayRequire="Van.Beasts">0.01</DA_NorthernDrog>
						<DA_ForestOwlcat MayRequire="Van.Beasts">0.15</DA_ForestOwlcat>
						<DA_RedhornedLarpah MayRequire="Van.Beasts">0.01</DA_RedhornedLarpah>
						<DA_Taraal MayRequire="Van.Beasts">0.03</DA_Taraal>
						<MA_Deermoss MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.03</MA_Deermoss>
						<MA_Direhorse MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.02</MA_Direhorse>
						<MA_Dunbear MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Dunbear>
						<MA_Duskhorn MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Duskhorn>
						<MA_Gnaut MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.1</MA_Gnaut>
						<MA_Hellboar MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Hellboar>
						<MA_Plastemmoth MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Plastemmoth>
						<MA_Raptorkhan MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.02</MA_Raptorkhan>
						<MA_Scarodon MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Scarodon>
						<MA_Sporemole MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.005</MA_Sporemole>
						<MA_Worhin MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.01</MA_Worhin>
					</value>
				</match>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

